From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: read the fixed GPU busy power counter

RBBM_PERFCTR_RBBM_1 is a selectable performance counter. Its default
selector is RBBM_ALWAYS_ON, so using it as busy time reports almost 100%
while clocks run and keeps devfreq at the maximum frequency regardless
of actual rendering load.

The existing RBBM_CTL enable and GPU_BUSY_MASKED setup initializes the
fixed PWR counter 1. Read that counter, matching Samsung's A3xx KGSL
busy_cycles implementation. The register descriptions distinguish PWR_1
at 0x00ec from the selectable RBBM_1 at 0x0094.

Source: LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226 at
3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256, adreno_a3xx.c busy_cycles.
Current upstream was checked 2026-10-13 and still uses RBBM_1.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
index 6831106a5..2f6aedf4f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
@@ -492,7 +492,8 @@ static u64 a3xx_gpu_busy(struct msm_gpu *gpu, unsigned long *out_sample_rate)
 {
 	u64 busy_cycles;
 
-	busy_cycles = gpu_read64(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_PERFCTR_RBBM_1_LO);
+	/* PWR counter 1 counts masked GPU busy cycles; RBBM counters are selectable. */
+	busy_cycles = gpu_read64(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_PERFCTR_PWR_1_LO);
 	*out_sample_rate = clk_get_rate(gpu->core_clk);
 
 	return busy_cycles;
-- 
